  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CR8">Exercise <span data-tag="0CR8">111.10.1</span>.</a> Compute the set of associated primes for each of the following modules. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R = k[x, y]$ and $M = R/(xy(x + y))$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R = \mathbf{Z}[x]$ and $M = R/(300x + 75)$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R = k[x, y, z]$ and $M = R/(x^3, x^2y, xz)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Here as usual $k$ is a field. </p>
